  "course_description": "An introduction to the art of ancient Egypt from the beginning of the New Kingdom to the conquest of Egypt by Rome.",
  "course_notes": "This course explores ancient Egyptian art from the beginning of the New Kingdom to the defeat of Cleopatra by Rome (1550-30 BCE). Structured chronologically, the course examines the uses and developments of ancient Egyptian art and architecture within their social, religious, and political contexts based on contemporary sources and archaeological excavation. The course includes visits to the Michael C. Carlos Museum galleries to view works from the various periods. Art History major/minor: Division I",
